\section*{Numerical-dimension-one log abundance in characteristic above three}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
For projective log-canonical threefold pairs in characteristic $p>3$, a nef rational adjoint of numerical dimension one is claimed to be semiample without terminality or factoriality assumptions. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 035, 2026-10-05): Boundary intersection control separates components from a primitive nef cycle by quantitative bend-and-break. The resulting connected Cartier divisor meets the companion cycle-obstruction hypotheses, ruling out the remaining zero-Kodaira case and giving semiampleness.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
Manuscript 1 (family 035, 2026-10-05): The problem selects the mathematical statement summarized here, including its stated hypotheses and parameter range. The cited theorem gives a claimed proof of that assertion in full.

\subsection{Formal verification}
